{#- The frame of every turn of the Intel Phi Cortex chat model: the format it is trained in (tools/chat-text.c),
    <|system|>TEXT<|end|>, <|user|>TEXT<|end|>, <|assistant|><|think|>REASONING<|/think|>ANSWER<|end|>, each marker
    one token of the chat BPE (tools/bpe.c), a newline after each <|end|>. Variables: messages (role system | user |
    assistant, content), identity (name), think (true: the model opens its think block itself; false: an empty block
    is given, the no-think form it was trained on too), add_generation_prompt. A system message, when given, comes
    first; without one, a short identity line stands in its place. Re-fed assistant turns carry no think block (the
    harness strips it, as Qwen's template does). The export `stop` is the string a reply ends before. -#}
{%- set stop = "<|end|>" -%}
{%- set name = identity.name | default("Cortex") -%}
{%- if messages | length == 0 or messages[0].role != "system" -%}
<|system|>You are {{ name }}, the Intel Phi Cortex: a small language model of one hundred and twenty columns on a Xeon Phi card. Answer plainly.<|end|>
{% endif -%}
{%- for m in messages -%}
{%- if m.role == "system" -%}
<|system|>{{ m.content | trim }}<|end|>
{% elif m.role == "user" -%}
<|user|>{{ m.content | trim }}<|end|>
{% else -%}
<|assistant|>{{ m.content | trim }}<|end|>
{% endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if add_generation_prompt -%}
<|assistant|>{% if not think %}<|think|><|/think|>{% endif %}
{%- endif -%}
